       "text": "I haven't entered this order. Ibuprofen 1600 mg four times daily comes to 6,400 mg/day, which is twice the maximum labeled daily dose for adults (3,200 mg/day). Each 1,600 mg dose is also double the usual maximum single dose of 800 mg. At this dose the risks of GI bleeding, kidney injury, and cardiovascular events go up substantially, even when kidney and liver function are normal.\n\nIt may be a typo. These are common intended regimens:\n- **800 mg by mouth, 4 times daily** (3,200 mg/day), which is the maximum for inflammatory conditions or severe pain.\n- **400\u2013600 mg by mouth, every 6 hours**, which is typical for analgesia.\n- **1600 mg total per day**, divided into 400 mg four times daily.\n\nIf you want one of these, tell me which and I'll enter it right away. If you really do intend 1600 mg four times daily, please confirm the clinical rationale. I'd also suggest checking with pharmacy first, because I can't verify the intent on my end."
